{
  "frozen_on": "2026-11-09",
  "frozen_against_engine": "bc7cf10dce35e595bfc9aaf79e484bf1a577c0a4",
  "rules": [
    "An expectation is FOUND when a finding outside test code sits in its file within `window` lines (default 2) of the anchor's line, whatever the rule id. It is FOUND AT MEDIUM OR ABOVE when that finding's rank is critical, high or medium.",
    "A `clean` expectation is a FALSE ALARM when any medium-or-above finding outside test code sits within its window.",
    "An expected finding COVERS A SECURITY PATH when the found finding has a `reachable` entry (a route, page or command reaches the flagged line).",
    "A vulnerable app is GIVEN A GREEN RELEASE when its release decision is Passed (readiness.json `release.decision` once it exists) or, before that, when it has no critical or high finding outside test code: that is what the badge and the evidence report show today.",
    "Call-site counts are Graph.call_sites() as stored in graph.json: raw counts per group, one denominator per app. A change in counting is not an improvement; the runner records the definition version of call_sites() it read.",
    "Nothing here is tuned to a fix: the public apps document their own problems (READMEs, solution guides, in-code 'Fix for' comments); the local apps were written from the directive's list of flows before any engine change, and the review examples are copied from the independent review of 2026-11-09.",
    "An `authz` expectation counts only findings whose rule id matches LW-AUTH|AUTH|authz|ACCESS|IDOR|BOLA|PERM: a shell or SQL finding on the same lines is a different problem."
  ],
